Sval: check for updates at Sval's static feed

Sval serves one update.xml per channel and platform from download.sval.app,
so the URL names only those two, and an update check tells the server
nothing else: not the version, build, OS version, locale or distribution.
The updater compares versions itself. The host has no configure option
(build/moz.build defaults MOZ_APPUPDATE_HOST to aus5.mozilla.org), and the
path is fixed here.

diff --git a/build/application.ini.in b/build/application.ini.in
index 6df1323..0cc766e 100644
--- a/build/application.ini.in
+++ b/build/application.ini.in
@@ -52,5 +52,5 @@ ServerURL=@MOZ_CRASHREPORTER_URL@/submit?id=@MOZ_APP_ID@&version=@MOZ_APP_VERSIO
 
 #if MOZ_UPDATER
 [AppUpdate]
-URL=https://@MOZ_APPUPDATE_HOST@/update/6/%PRODUCT%/%VERSION%/%BUILD_ID%/%BUILD_TARGET%/%LOCALE%/%CHANNEL%/%OS_VERSION%/%SYSTEM_CAPABILITIES%/%DISTRIBUTION%/%DISTRIBUTION_VERSION%/update.xml
+URL=https://download.sval.app/update/1/%CHANNEL%/%BUILD_TARGET%/update.xml
 #endif
